1
00:00:00,266 --> 00:00:03,000
很多学中文的人问我
Hěn duō xué zhōngwén de rén wèn wǒ
Many people learning Chinese ask me

2
00:00:03,166 --> 00:00:06,366
我要不要学习语法呢
Wǒ yào bù yào xuéxí yǔfǎ ne
Should I study grammar?

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,400
感觉语法很重要
Gǎnjué yǔfǎ hěn zhòngyào
It feels like grammar is important

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,533
我是不是要努力学语法
Wǒ shì bù shì yào nǔlì xué yǔfǎ
Should I work hard to learn grammar?

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:18,166
还有的学生问我
Hái yǒu de xuéshēng wèn wǒ
Some students also ask me

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:22,500
感觉中文有很多句子结构
Gǎnjué zhōngwén yǒu hěn duō jùzi jiégòu
It feels like Chinese has many sentence structures

7
00:00:23,266 --> 00:00:24,400
那
Nà
So

8
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:29,600
我想要说更长的更复杂的句子
Wǒ xiǎng yào shuō gèng cháng de gèng fùzá de jùzi
I want to say longer, more complex sentences

9
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:32,866
是不是我要学习语法
Shì bù shì wǒ yào xuéxí yǔfǎ
Does that mean I should study grammar?

10
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,400
然后学习怎么用它们呢
Ránhòu xuéxí zěnme yòng tāmen ne
And learn how to use them?

11
00:00:36,766 --> 00:00:39,366
今天我用这个视频
Jīntiān wǒ yòng zhè ge shìpín
Today I’m using this video

12
00:00:39,533 --> 00:00:44,366
来回答你们关于语法的问题
Lái huídá nǐmen guānyú yǔfǎ de wèntí
To answer your questions about grammar

13
00:00:44,566 --> 00:00:46,300
在开始之前
Zài kāishǐ zhīqián
Before we start

14
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:48,166
我要告诉大家
Wǒ yào gàosu dàjiā
I want to tell you all

15
00:00:48,366 --> 00:00:52,566
你可以打开这个视频的字幕
Nǐ kěyǐ dǎkāi zhè ge shìpín de zìmù
You can turn on subtitles for this video

16
00:00:53,266 --> 00:00:58,533
你可以看中文和英语的字幕一起
Nǐ kěyǐ kàn zhōngwén hé yīngyǔ de zìmù yìqǐ
You can watch both Chinese and English subtitles together

17
00:00:58,733 --> 00:01:01,333
你可以用一个Chrome extension
Nǐ kěyǐ yòng yí gè Chrome extension
You can use a Chrome extension

18
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:03,266
叫language reactor
Jiào language reactor
Called Language Reactor

19
00:01:03,466 --> 00:01:06,200
如果你不知道你不会
Rúguǒ nǐ bù zhīdào nǐ bú huì
If you don’t know how to use it

20
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,666
那你可以看这个视频的下面的说明
Nà nǐ kěyǐ kàn zhè ge shìpín de xiàmiàn de shuōmíng
Then you can look at the description below this video

21
00:01:11,166 --> 00:01:15,166
那我要先跟你说一个故事
Nà wǒ yào xiān gēn nǐ shuō yí gè gùshì
Let me first tell you a story

22
00:01:15,166 --> 00:01:17,200
我是一个中国人
Wǒ shì yí gè Zhōngguó rén
I am Chinese

23
00:01:17,366 --> 00:01:19,933
我从小学习英语
Wǒ cóng xiǎo xuéxí Yīngyǔ
I studied English from a young age

24
00:01:20,566 --> 00:01:25,900
中国人一般会从7岁开始学
Zhōngguó rén yìbān huì cóng qī suì kāishǐ xué
Usually, Chinese people start learning at 7 years old

25
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:27,600
现在更早
Xiànzài gèng zǎo
Now it starts even earlier

26
00:01:28,066 --> 00:01:31,600
从7岁可能学到20岁
Cóng qī suì kěnéng xué dào èrshí suì
You might study from age 7 all the way to 20

27
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,166
学习十多年
Xuéxí shí duō nián
Study for over ten years

28
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,800
很长时间
Hěn cháng shíjiān
A very long time

29
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:36,600
对不对
Duì bù duì
Right?

30
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:42,866
那我呢在中国有过很多英语老师
Nà wǒ ne zài Zhōngguó yǒu guò hěn duō Yīngyǔ lǎoshī
In China, I had many English teachers

31
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,966
他们都有一个一样的地方
Tāmen dōu yǒu yí gè yíyàng de dìfang
They all had one thing in common

32
00:01:46,366 --> 00:01:50,000
就是他们都知道很多语法
Jiùshì tāmen dōu zhīdào hěn duō yǔfǎ
They all knew a lot of grammar

33
00:01:50,466 --> 00:01:54,300
然后他们教我们很多语法点
Ránhòu tāmen jiāo wǒmen hěn duō yǔfǎ diǎn
And they taught us many grammar points

34
00:01:55,133 --> 00:01:56,000
所以
Suǒyǐ
So

35
00:01:56,066 --> 00:02:01,733
中国的学生知道很多英语的语法点
Zhōngguó de xuéshēng zhīdào hěn duō Yīngyǔ de yǔfǎ diǎn
Chinese students know a lot of English grammar rules

36
00:02:02,066 --> 00:02:03,600
比如说什么呢
Bǐrú shuō shénme ne
For example?

37
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:09,266
被动句、时态和 if 条件句
Bèidòng jù, shítài hé if tiáojiàn jù
Passive voice, tenses, and if-conditional sentences

38
00:02:09,266 --> 00:02:10,766
很多很多很多
Hěn duō hěn duō hěn duō
Many, many, many

39
00:02:10,933 --> 00:02:14,366
你觉得中国人的英语好吗
Nǐ juéde Zhōngguó rén de Yīngyǔ hǎo ma
Do you think Chinese people are good at English?

40
00:02:14,566 --> 00:02:16,566
如果你去过中国
Rúguǒ nǐ qù guò Zhōngguó
If you've been to China

41
00:02:16,666 --> 00:02:20,466
你知道中国人的英语很烂
Nǐ zhīdào Zhōngguó rén de Yīngyǔ hěn làn
You know their English is really bad

42
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:22,866
对不对 很垃圾
Duì bù duì hěn lājī
Right? Really trash

43
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:27,066
中国人真的不能说英语
Zhōngguó rén zhēn de bù néng shuō Yīngyǔ
Chinese people really can’t speak English

44
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,466
也听不懂英语
Yě tīng bù dǒng Yīngyǔ
They can’t understand it either

45
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,933
你现在在学习中文
Nǐ xiànzài zài xuéxí Zhōngwén
You’re learning Chinese now

46
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:33,966
那你可能知道
Nà nǐ kěnéng zhīdào
So you probably know

47
00:02:34,166 --> 00:02:37,733
如果一个人他的中文不太好
Rúguǒ yí gè rén tā de Zhōngwén bù tài hǎo
If someone’s Chinese isn’t good

48
00:02:37,933 --> 00:02:41,300
可能一个人去中国旅游
Kěnéng yí gè rén qù Zhōngguó lǚyóu
If someone travels to China

49
00:02:41,533 --> 00:02:43,466
会有很多问题
Huì yǒu hěn duō wèntí
There will be a lot of problems

50
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:47,266
因为中国人听不懂英语
Yīnwèi Zhōngguó rén tīng bù dǒng Yīngyǔ
Because Chinese people don’t understand English

51
00:02:47,366 --> 00:02:49,933
你说什么他们都听不懂
Nǐ shuō shénme tāmen dōu tīng bù dǒng
They don’t understand anything you say

52
00:02:50,266 --> 00:02:53,700
他们也不会用英语跟你说话
Tāmen yě bú huì yòng Yīngyǔ gēn nǐ shuōhuà
And they won’t speak to you in English

53
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:57,766
所以中国人的英语真的非常差
Suǒyǐ Zhōngguó rén de Yīngyǔ zhēn de fēicháng chà
So Chinese people’s English is really very poor

54
00:02:58,066 --> 00:03:01,200
所以你的语法学得很好
Suǒyǐ nǐ de yǔfǎ xué de hěn hǎo
So even if you learn grammar very well

55
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:04,066
或者你知道很多语法
Huòzhě nǐ zhīdào hěn duō yǔfǎ
Or you know a lot of grammar

56
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:08,266
跟你会说很好的中文
Gēn nǐ huì shuō hěn hǎo de Zhōngwén
It doesn’t necessarily mean you can speak Chinese well

57
00:03:08,533 --> 00:03:10,333
你能听得懂很多
Nǐ néng tīng de dǒng hěn duō
Or understand a lot

58
00:03:10,466 --> 00:03:12,533
我觉得关系不大
Wǒ juéde guānxì bù dà
I think there isn’t much of a connection

59
00:03:12,966 --> 00:03:15,733
因为有这么多的中国人
Yīnwèi yǒu zhème duō de Zhōngguó rén
Because so many Chinese people

60
00:03:15,733 --> 00:03:17,900
都知道这么多语法
Dōu zhīdào zhème duō yǔfǎ
Know so much grammar

61
00:03:18,066 --> 00:03:20,900
可是他们还是不会说
Kěshì tāmen háishì bú huì shuō
But they still can’t speak

62
00:03:20,933 --> 00:03:24,100
这么多中国人已经给我们证明了
Zhème duō Zhōngguó rén yǐjīng gěi wǒmen zhèngmíng le
All these Chinese people have already proven to us

63
00:03:24,566 --> 00:03:29,866
语法和你的说话和听力的关系不大
Yǔfǎ hé nǐ de shuōhuà hé tīnglì de guānxì bù dà
Grammar has little to do with your speaking and listening ability

64
00:03:29,966 --> 00:03:33,566
那语法就完全没有用了吗
Nà yǔfǎ jiù wánquán méiyǒu yòng le ma
So does that mean grammar is completely useless?

65
00:03:33,966 --> 00:03:37,866
不，语法还是可以帮助得到你
Bù, yǔfǎ háishì kěyǐ bāngzhù de dào nǐ
No, grammar can still help you

66
00:03:38,566 --> 00:03:41,966
但是语法有多重要呢
Dànshì yǔfǎ yǒu duō zhòngyào ne
But how important is grammar?

67
00:03:42,333 --> 00:03:45,500
还有你可以怎么学习它们呢
Hái yǒu nǐ kěyǐ zěnme xuéxí tāmen ne
And how can you study it?

68
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:49,966
那今天我要告诉你一个假说
Nà jīntiān wǒ yào gàosu nǐ yí gè jiǎshuō
Today I want to share with you a hypothesis

69
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:54,166
我相信这个假说可以给你答案
Wǒ xiāngxìn zhè gè jiǎshuō kěyǐ gěi nǐ dá’àn
I believe this hypothesis can give you an answer

70
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,666
那这个假设呢
Nà zhè gè jiǎshè ne
This hypothesis

71
00:03:56,700 --> 00:04:00,466
是一个很有名的语言学家
Shì yí gè hěn yǒumíng de yǔyán xuéjiā
Was proposed by a famous linguist

72
00:04:00,566 --> 00:04:02,366
叫Stephen Krashen
Jiào Stephen Krashen
Named Stephen Krashen

73
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:05,400
他的监控假设
Tā de jiānkòng jiǎshè
His Monitor Hypothesis

74
00:04:05,566 --> 00:04:08,566
那在这个监控假设里啊
Nà zài zhè ge jiānkòng jiǎshè lǐ a
In this Monitor Hypothesis

75
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:12,566
他说我们在学习一个语言的时候
Tā shuō wǒmen zài xuéxí yí gè yǔyán de shíhou
He says that when we are learning a language

76
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,200
我们说的时候
Wǒmen shuō de shíhou
When we speak

77
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:19,133
主要是用我们习得的知识
Zhǔyào shì yòng wǒmen xídé de zhīshi
We mainly use the knowledge we have acquired

78
00:04:19,166 --> 00:04:22,800
语法呢 是你学习的语法
Yǔfǎ ne shì nǐ xuéxí de yǔfǎ
Grammar is something you have consciously studied

79
00:04:22,933 --> 00:04:24,400
学习的语法呢
Xuéxí de yǔfǎ ne
Studied grammar

80
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:28,766
只能帮助你去检查你的错误
Zhǐ néng bāngzhù nǐ qù jiǎnchá nǐ de cuòwù
Can only help you check your mistakes

81
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:31,733
改正你说的东西
Gǎizhèng nǐ shuō de dōngxi
And correct what you said

82
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,333
那习得是什么意思呢
Nà xídé shì shénme yìsi ne
So what does "acquire" mean?

83
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:39,366
习得是你潜意识里学习到的东西
Xídé shì nǐ qiǎnyìshí lǐ xuéxí dào de dōngxi
Acquisition is what you learn subconsciously

84
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:42,400
嗯 是你看了很多中文
Ńg, shì nǐ kàn le hěn duō zhōngwén
It’s from watching a lot of Chinese

85
00:04:42,733 --> 00:04:44,766
你听了很多中文
Nǐ tīng le hěn duō zhōngwén
And listening to a lot of Chinese

86
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:49,933
你自然地会说 会用一些中文
Nǐ zìrán de huì shuō, huì yòng yìxiē zhōngwén
You naturally start to speak and use some Chinese

87
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,666
这个是你习得的中文
Zhè ge shì nǐ xídé de zhōngwén
That is the Chinese you have acquired

88
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:56,800
而不是你坐在桌子面前啊
Ér bù shì nǐ zuò zài zhuōzi miànqián a
It’s not from sitting in front of a desk

89
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,866
看这个语法规则
Kàn zhè ge yǔfǎ guīzé
And looking at grammar rules

90
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,200
这个是你的意识在学习语法规则
Zhè ge shì nǐ de yìshí zài xuéxí yǔfǎ guīzé
That is your conscious mind studying grammar

91
00:05:03,366 --> 00:05:06,266
不是你习得的中文
Bù shì nǐ xídé de zhōngwén
It’s not the Chinese you’ve acquired

92
00:05:06,566 --> 00:05:07,400
说到这个
Shuō dào zhè ge
Speaking of this

93
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:09,566
我觉得很对
Wǒ juéde hěn duì
I think that’s very true

94
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:14,500
因为我自己觉得我的英语还不错
Yīnwèi wǒ zìjǐ juéde wǒ de Yīngyǔ hái búcuò
Because I think my English is pretty good

95
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:17,200
那我在中国
Nà wǒ zài Zhōngguó
So when I was in China

96
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:20,400
我小的时候学英语的时候
Wǒ xiǎo de shíhou xué Yīngyǔ de shíhou
When I studied English as a child

97
00:05:20,733 --> 00:05:23,700
每次老师讲语法
Měi cì lǎoshī jiǎng yǔfǎ
Every time the teacher talked about grammar

98
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:26,200
我就我不听我不听我不听
Wǒ jiù wǒ bù tīng wǒ bù tīng wǒ bù tīng
I would go “I’m not listening, I’m not listening”

99
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:28,100
因为我也听不懂
Yīnwèi wǒ yě tīng bù dǒng
Because I didn’t understand it either

100
00:05:28,266 --> 00:05:30,733
我觉得让这个语言更难
Wǒ juéde ràng zhè ge yǔyán gèng nán
I felt like it made the language harder

101
00:05:31,133 --> 00:05:35,066
但是我很喜欢去听很多英语歌
Dànshì wǒ hěn xǐhuān qù tīng hěn duō Yīngyǔ gē
But I really liked listening to a lot of English songs

102
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,133
英语的电影
Yīngyǔ de diànyǐng
English movies

103
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,666
如果是英语的我都喜欢
Rúguǒ shì Yīngyǔ de wǒ dōu xǐhuān
If it was in English, I liked it all

104
00:05:39,666 --> 00:05:42,900
我喜欢听人用英语说话
Wǒ xǐhuān tīng rén yòng Yīngyǔ shuōhuà
I liked listening to people speak English

105
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,500
然后呢我说英语的时候
Ránhòu ne wǒ shuō Yīngyǔ de shíhou
And then, when I spoke English

106
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:49,266
就有一种感觉就是
Jiù yǒu yì zhǒng gǎnjué jiùshì
I had this feeling that

107
00:05:49,266 --> 00:05:50,900
我不知道语法
Wǒ bù zhīdào yǔfǎ
I didn’t know the grammar

108
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:53,666
但是我感觉这样说很自然
Dànshì wǒ gǎnjué zhèyàng shuō hěn zìrán
But I felt this way of saying it was natural

109
00:05:53,866 --> 00:05:55,400
这样说是对的
Zhèyàng shuō shì duì de
This way of speaking was correct

110
00:05:55,566 --> 00:05:59,400
然后在 Stephen Krashen 的监控假设里
Ránhòu zài Stephen Krashen de jiānkòng jiǎshè lǐ
Then in Stephen Krashen’s Monitor Hypothesis

111
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,733
他说
Tā shuō
He says

112
00:06:00,733 --> 00:06:05,200
监控不能帮助学习的人说得很流利
Jiānkòng bù néng bāngzhù xuéxí de rén shuō de hěn liúlì
The monitor can’t help learners speak fluently

113
00:06:05,566 --> 00:06:08,333
但是它只是能用来帮你调整
Dànshì tā zhǐshì néng yòng lái bāng nǐ tiáozhěng
It’s only used to help you adjust

114
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:09,966
还有修正你的句子
Hái yǒu xiūzhèng nǐ de jùzi
And correct your sentences

115
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,600
然后他说
Ránhòu tā shuō
Then he says

116
00:06:11,966 --> 00:06:13,866
监控假设呢
Jiānkòng jiǎshè ne
The Monitor Hypothesis

117
00:06:13,866 --> 00:06:18,600
是不能帮你说一口流利的语言的
Shì bù néng bāng nǐ shuō yì kǒu liúlì de yǔyán de
Can’t help you speak a fluent language

118
00:06:19,133 --> 00:06:23,166
它是用来帮你检查你说的东西
Tā shì yòng lái bāng nǐ jiǎnchá nǐ shuō de dōngxi
It’s used to help you check what you’re saying

119
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,700
还有改你说的东西
Hái yǒu gǎi nǐ shuō de dōngxi
And correct what you’re saying

120
00:06:25,966 --> 00:06:27,900
把它说成对的
Bǎ tā shuō chéng duì de
Make it correct

121
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:30,266
这个我觉得很有道理
Zhè ge wǒ juéde hěn yǒu dàolǐ
I think this makes a lot of sense

122
00:06:30,466 --> 00:06:33,766
因为你在学习中文的时候
Yīnwèi nǐ zài xuéxí Zhōngwén de shíhou
